# Neo Learn Sampler parameters (docs/specs/neo-learn.md, neo-learn-controls.md A1 and A2.7). The order is permanent: songs and
# presets store values by position. The 12 controls are the six core ones, then the six global ones (Attack, Decay, Sustain, Release,
# Unison / Spread, Output). Each has a snake_case id, and the Explain text (How, Sound; the description is the How line).
# Regenerate: python3 tools/gen-machine-params.py Machines/NeoLearnSampler
namespace NeoBuzz.LearnSampler
class NeoLearnSamplerMachine
tracks 16
summary Teaching sampler: one Dye Essence patch driven by 12 controls. One sample (Dye's five built-in ones, or your own WAV) played across the keyboard, with a start offset past the attack, a tone tilt around 1 kHz, a crossfaded loop, a vintage grit stage (12 bits, a lower sample rate, tape wow) and a small room, with an ADSR, unison and an output gain. Every control says what it does and what you will hear. Use it for lo-fi keys, pads and drones from a sample, or to learn how a sampler shapes one recording.
import sample .wav | A WAV sample (mono or stereo, up to 20 s, kept in the machine state): the sample the Source control's User choice plays

group Core
SampleOffset     "Start Offset" 0 1000 0 pct
    id sample_offset
    how Moves the sample playback start point forward past the initial recorded attack transient.
    sound At 0% you hear the full natural hammer/pluck attack; raising it removes the transient for smooth, pad-like swells.

TimbreTilt       "Tone" 0 1000 500 bip
    id timbre_tilt
    how Tilts the spectrum around 1 kHz: a gentle low-pass to the left, a high shelf to the right.
    sound Left sounds soft and dark, like a gentle touch; right sounds bright and present.

Source           "Source" 0 5 0 enum Choir Strings Bell Pluck Texture User
    id source
    how Selects the sample played across the keyboard: Dye Essence's `Choir`, `Strings`, `Bell`, `Pluck`, `Texture`, or `User`, a WAV you load.
    sound Changes the raw material every other control shapes.

Loop             "Loop" 0 1000 0 pct
    id loop
    how 0% plays the sample once from the start offset; above 0% it loops a region after the offset, crossfaded, whose length grows with the value.
    sound One-shot sounds stay natural; looping turns any sample into a sustained pad or drone.

VintageDac       "Vintage Grit" 0 1000 0 pct
    id vintage_dac
    how Engages 12-bit amplitude quantization, sample-rate reduction, and subtle tape wow/flutter.
    sound Transforms pristine studio recordings into nostalgic 90s hardware sampler and lo-fi tape textures.

RoomSpace        "Room Acoustic" 0 1000 200 pct
    id room_space
    how Blends in stereo early reflections and natural studio room decay around the dry samples.
    sound Places the instrument inside a realistic physical recording space rather than sounding dry and direct.

group Global
EnvAttack        "Attack" 0 1000 300 time 0.0005 5
    id env_attack
    how Sets the time required for the note's amplitude (and routed envelope modulation) to ramp from silence to full peak after a note-on trigger.
    sound Low values create immediate, percussive plucks; high values produce slow, swelling pads.
EnvDecay         "Decay" 0 1000 600 time 0.005 8
    id env_decay
    how Controls how long it takes for the signal to drop from peak level down to the sustain level while a key remains held.
    sound Short decay makes notes snappy and tight; longer decay gives a gradual piano- or bell-like fade.
EnvSustain       "Sustain" 0 1000 800 pct
    id env_sustain
    how Defines the steady-state volume level maintained for as long as a note is held after the Attack and Decay stages complete.
    sound At 0% the synth behaves like a plucked or struck instrument; at 100% it holds full organ-like volume.
EnvRelease       "Release" 0 1000 500 time 0.005 10
    id env_release
    how Sets the time required for the sound to fade from its current level to complete silence after the note is released.
    sound Short release stops notes abruptly; long release leaves an ambient tail that blends chords together.
UnisonDetune     "Unison / Spread" 0 1000 0 pct
    id unison_detune
    how 0% plays one voice per note; above 0% each note plays 5 detuned, stereo-spread voices (3 in Additive, Granular and Spectral), with detune (up to ±50 cents) and width growing with the value.
    sound Thickens thin waveforms into wide, chorus-like stereo leads and pads.
OutputGain       "Output" 0 1000 665 db -36 12
    id output_gain
    how Sets the level after synthesis. There is no limiter (NeoBuzz mixes in floating point); a clip light shows when the output passes 0 dBFS.
    sound Controls overall loudness; keep the clip light dark when the next machine expects levels at or below 0 dBFS.

# What the machine measures (NeoLearnSamplerMachine.Readings, machine_readings): the output after Output, in dBFS.
reading rms_db dB | The output's RMS over about half a second (-inf: silence)
reading peak_db dB | The output's peak, falling 20 dB a second (-inf: silence)
reading active_voices notes | Notes sounding now (unison voices belong to their note)
